From 46863dfbd3e7d51676b9030b279426ae8ee324df Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jozsef Kiraly <fonix232@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 05:07:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 5/5] board: qnap: 301w: A/B boot flow with fallback and rescue

Add the board directory with the default environment and a small
ft_system_setup() hook:

- two firmware slots (GPT partitions fit_a/fit_b), each one FIT image
  read in full (imszb) and verified (iminfo) before bootm
- the active slot comes from boot_slot; if it is missing or fails
  verification the other slot is booted and becomes active
- a boot counter (bootlimit, altbootcmd) switches slots when one keeps
  failing to come up, and falls back to rescue if the other does too
- rescue boots an initramfs from USB, then TFTP, and retries forever;
  holding the reset button at power-on goes there directly
- ft_system_setup() copies /chosen/rootdisk-<slot> to /chosen/rootdisk
  for the kernel's fitblk driver, like OpenWrt's MediaTek boards

The environment lives in the ubootenv GPT partition, located through
the device tree with CONFIG_ENV_MMC_USE_DT so that a missing partition
disables saving instead of writing to a raw offset of the eMMC.
